Package: pipi
Title: Political Inequality in Participation Index
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Pál", family = "Susánszky",
           email = "susanszky.pal@tk.hu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Róbert", family = "Somogyi", role = "aut"),
    person(given = "Gergely", family = "Tóth", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Computes the Political Inequality in Participation Index (PIPI),
    a generalized-Gini-based index of inequalities in political participation.
    Supports respondent-level data with optional fixed survey weights and
    aggregated integer group counts. Estimates the GEGINI expected under
    random allocation of the observed number of participants, determines a
    feasible maximum, and offers an independent and identically distributed
    nonparametric bootstrap for uncertainty assessment. Uses only R's bundled
    base and recommended packages. The index was introduced by
    Susánszky, Somogyi and Tóth (2023) <doi:10.1177/10434631221143614>.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats, utils, graphics
NeedsCompilation: no
URL: https://doi.org/10.1177/10434631221143614
